     This iinniitt does not run a separate fsck-style check before
     entering single-user mode; instead, the writability of the
     root file system is probed directly by attempting to create
     /eettcc/bboooottttiimmee. While root remains read-only, iinniitt refuses to
     run /eettcc/rrcc and stays in single-user mode.
